    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493310009/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """her husband’s lips as he reads aloud the works of --- Vernon Lee!! It is too good to be true, but it is true. Placci says he wonders what Vernon, who longs to be ‘kept before the Public’, thinks of being kept before something that isn’t public yet!
Lina and her husband arrived in the evening. Horne also came to dinner. Lina seemed well and happy, but she entirely takes the lead. It is curious to see B.B.’s and Venetia Cowper’s view justified, that in her marriage she had followed her Aunt’s example and taken another Carlo Orsi. 
Nov. 6. 1902.. I Tatti Thursday
Wasted my morning writing notes of no real importance - Donna Rezia, Mrs. Morgan, the Platonoff, Mrs.  Muchau , Miss Zocco, Gertrude, Karin (who is better), Gertrude, etc. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 80 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1902-03> .

